{%- comment -%}
Normalises one route, whichever units and shape it was written in.

A route is a *course*; an `efforts:` list holds the dated times run on it. A
one-off race can skip `efforts:` and carry a flat `time:` and `dates:` — that
is treated as a single effort, so both shapes work side by side.

Where a recurring race moved its course between years, the effort carries its
own `gpx:` and overrides the route's. Only one track is ever drawn per route
(see route_primary_gpx) so re-runs of the same course do not stack up.

Everything below is metric and seconds; miles, feet, and minutes are input and
display forms only. Elevation and pace keep a decimal place rather than being
rounded here, so that _js/units.js converting them to feet or minutes per mile
lands on the figure the author wrote down, not one a rounding step away.

Sets, for the caller:
  route_km route_m               distance and elevation gain
  route_sec route_has_seconds    the best recorded time, and its precision
  route_sec_per_km route_pace    pace derived from that time: exact seconds
                                 per km, and the rounded m:ss string
  route_effort_count             how many times it has been run
  route_latest_date              most recent outing
  route_primary_gpx              the single track to draw, if any

Jekyll leaks every `assign` in an include back to the caller, so these working
names are also left behind and should be treated as clobbered: route_efforts,
newest_effort, newest_gpx, primary_gpx, pace_whole, pace_minutes, pace_seconds,
and — via routes/parse_time.liquid — parsed_sec, parsed_precise, clock,
clock_h, clock_m, clock_s.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if include.route.distance_mi -%}
  {%- assign route_km = include.route.distance_mi | times: 1.609344 | round: 2 -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign route_km = include.route.distance_km | default: 0 | round: 2 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if include.route.elevation_ft -%}
  {%- assign route_m = include.route.elevation_ft | times: 0.3048 | round: 1 -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign route_m = include.route.elevation_m | default: 0 | round: 1 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign route_sec = 0 -%}
{%- assign route_has_seconds = false -%}
{%- assign route_effort_count = 0 -%}
{%- assign route_latest_date = nil -%}
{%- assign route_primary_gpx = include.route.gpx -%}

{%- if include.route.efforts -%}
  {%- assign route_efforts = include.route.efforts | sort: "date" -%}
  {%- assign route_effort_count = route_efforts | size -%}
  {%- assign newest_effort = route_efforts | last -%}
  {%- assign route_latest_date = newest_effort.date -%}

  {%- comment -%}
  One pass: the headline time is the fastest effort, and the drawn track is the
  newest effort that has one — unless an effort is marked `primary: true`, which
  wins outright. The two track candidates are kept apart and resolved after the
  loop so a primary effort is not overwritten by a later one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign newest_gpx = nil -%}
  {%- assign primary_gpx = nil -%}
  {%- for effort in route_efforts -%}
    {%- include routes/parse_time.liquid time=effort.time duration_min=effort.duration_min -%}
    {%- if parsed_sec > 0 -%}
      {%- if route_sec == 0 or parsed_sec < route_sec -%}
        {%- assign route_sec = parsed_sec -%}
        {%- assign route_has_seconds = parsed_precise -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if effort.gpx -%}
      {%- assign newest_gpx = effort.gpx -%}
      {%- if effort.primary -%}{%- assign primary_gpx = effort.gpx -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if primary_gpx -%}
    {%- assign route_primary_gpx = primary_gpx -%}
  {%- elsif newest_gpx -%}
    {%- assign route_primary_gpx = newest_gpx -%}
  {%- endif -%}

{%- else -%}
  {%- include routes/parse_time.liquid time=include.route.time duration_min=include.route.duration_min -%}
  {%- assign route_sec = parsed_sec -%}
  {%- assign route_has_seconds = parsed_precise -%}
  {%- if include.route.dates -%}
    {%- assign route_effort_count = include.route.dates | size -%}
    {%- assign route_latest_date = include.route.dates | sort | last -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign route_sec_per_km = 0 -%}
{%- assign route_pace = "—" -%}
{%- if route_sec > 0 and route_km > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  Liquid picks integer or float division from the operand types, so a distance
  written as a whole number would floor the pace by up to a second per km.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign route_km_exact = route_km | times: 1.0 -%}
  {%- assign route_sec_per_km = route_sec | divided_by: route_km_exact | round: 2 -%}
  {%- assign pace_whole = route_sec_per_km | round -%}
  {%- assign pace_minutes = pace_whole | divided_by: 60 -%}
  {%- assign pace_seconds = pace_whole | modulo: 60 | prepend: "0" | slice: -2, 2 -%}
  {%- assign route_pace = pace_minutes | append: ":" | append: pace_seconds -%}
{%- endif -%}
